"notes": "Modified cash basis city with accrual-basis enterprise funds. The trimmed PDF has no governmental funds receipts/disbursements statement (and no nonmajor fund pages), so governmental receipts/disbursements come from the government-wide Statement of Activities (p2-3), governmental activities column; program revenues listed by function, general revenues by line. Statement of Activities expenses include 166,210 depreciation, and net position includes capital assets, so a cash roll-forward is not possible: beginning cash is not shown (null) and reconcile will not tie. For reference, net position roll: 2,831,729 + 917,993 - 804,549 - 22,100 = 2,923,073 (governmental activities, p3); business-type 819,261 + 243,926 - 277,172 + 22,100 = 808,115. ending_cash is the sum of governmental cash, CDs, county treasurer cash and restricted cash on p1. Transfers: the proprietary statement (p5) labels 22,100 'Transfers to other funds' but it is added in the change in net position and shown as an inflow in cash flows (p7); governmental column on p3 shows (22,100); recorded as business_type.transfers_net +22,100 and governmental transfers_out 22,100. Budget schedules show GF transfers in 8,549 (Park 6,220 + Pool 2,329 on p12), Street transfers in 28,144, Sales Tax Fund transfers out 28,144; the 8,549 sending fund is not in the trimmed pages. Statement of Cash Flows p6 covers Water only; p7 has Sewer, Trash and Total columns (Total used). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p8) not recorded separately because the departmental combining statement (p11-12) is more detailed and has the same totals (608,646 / 614,180); in the departments statement Community Building column's sales tax 34,072 and Capital outlay under General/Park; Statement of Activities function split ties. Street and Sales Tax Fund budget schedules recorded. Read pages 1-13 of 13",
